        <mxCell id="c66" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=13;" value="Series, as built. Each tank is blended against a bypass that goes around it.&#xa;The knob is &quot;+ %Long Tank&quot;, linear 0% to 100%.&#xa;Hard left  = + 0% Long   : short tank and the Gain / Dirt block on their own.&#xa;Noon       = + 50% Long  : half the signal cascaded on through the long tank.&#xa;Hard right = + 100% Long : all of it through the long tank.&#xa;NOTE: the +6 dB makeup sits before the long tank at EVERY knob position, so the&#xa;hard-right (long only) end runs about 6 dB hotter than the hard-left (short only) end.&#xa;NOTE: the long tank keeps convolving even when it is mixed all the way out." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="1100" x="60" y="680" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
