        <mxCell id="c98" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=13;" value="Orange = spring tank convolution.   Blue = stereo stage.   Green = per channel.   Yellow = a gain.   Purple diamond = a sum.   Purple dashed = a path that skips a stage.&#xa;Blend knob: &quot;+ %Long Tank&quot;, 0% to 100%, linear the whole way. 0% is the short tank and the Gain / Dirt block on their own, 100% is all of it through the long tank.&#xa;Lines that cross without joining are drawn with a hop over the line underneath.&#xa;Comp / Off / Limit now sits in the feedback RETURN leg, between Feedback Fb% and Fb In, not in the wet path, so its job is taming the feedback loop. Both thresholds start at -24 dBFS." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="1700" x="60" y="880" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
