        <mxCell id="c80" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=13;" value="Orange = spring tank convolution.   Blue = stereo stage.   Green = per channel.   Yellow = a gain.   Purple diamond = a sum.   Purple dashed = a path that skips a stage.&#xa;Blend knob: &quot;Short / Long Tank Mix&quot;, reading x% Short / 100-x% Long. A straight crossfade between the two tank pairs, and the two always add up to 100%.&#xa;Lines that cross without joining are drawn with a hop over the line underneath.&#xa;Comp / Off / Limit now sits in the feedback RETURN leg, between Feedback Fb% and Fb In, not in the wet path, so its job is taming the feedback loop. Both thresholds start at -24 dBFS." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="1700" x="60" y="880" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="z9" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffcccc;strokeColor=#b85450;" value="Dirt (Gain pull)&amp;#10;TS808, TL072H&amp;#10;1N4148W pair&amp;#10;&amp;#10;+9VC&amp;#10;clips at +/-4.5 V" vertex="1">
